# Check text files out with LF everywhere, including Windows, where Git's
# default autocrlf would otherwise hand them back with CRLF. Committed
# artifacts are compared byte-for-byte against freshly generated output — see
# the `schema/config.schema.json` drift guard in core/tests/config_schema_drift.rs
# — and a rewritten line ending makes an identical file look stale.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Hand-built PDF test fixtures have no NUL bytes; without this, Git treats them
# as text and rewrites LF->CRLF on autocrlf checkouts, shifting xref offsets and
# stream /Length counts and corrupting the fixtures. Force binary handling.
*.pdf binary
